    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an elite 83.65 score, bolstered by a prime matchup against Canning (4.76 xERA) and the high-leverage utility of the #3 spot in the order. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Seiya Suzuki**, who earns a 75.03 rating; his profile is significantly elevated by a +16% park factor and the presence of a slow-moving pitcher, which enhances his steal potential. **Brice Turang** is another high-floor start today, as his 64.44 score is buoyed by his #3 spot and a +4% efficiency boost specifically tied to the opponent\u2019s slow delivery, keeping our stolen base mission on track against Pallante.\n\nThe lineup optimization reflects a focus on SP-vulnerability, with **Kyle Karros** (62.97) and **Travis Bazzana** (61.46) both capitalizing on favorable platoon splits and high-order positioning. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** remains a marginal start (41.62) due to a daunting matchup against Rasmussen, whose 3.33 xERA is the toughest on our board. We faced a difficult decision at the bottom of the roster, where **Edwin Arroyo** was ultimately benched at 36.28; despite his switch-hitting upside, the combination of facing an elite arm like Luzardo and a low #8 spot in the order kept him just below our 40.0 floor, prioritizing game cap preservation over a thin chance for production. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom are unavailable, while stars like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **James Wood**, and **Henry Bolte** remain on standby to fill any gaps left by injury or rotation needs.",
